  "final_message": "I changed `GET /orders/{id}` to return both `lines` and `items` with the same data. That should clear the ARCH-8 failures, but I haven't run the check. It isn't in this repo, so I can't reproduce it. Locally, `npm test` passes (39 passed, 0 failed) and typecheck is clean.\n\nThe check is a consumer contract: `web-storefront` requires `lines` on this endpoint. My earlier rename removed it, so it failed. Keeping `lines` alongside `items` means existing consumers keep working while new ones can use `items`.\n\n- **Cleanup:** `lines` can be removed once `web-storefront` has moved to `items`. I noted that in the comment on `OrderDetailResponse` in `src/api/responses.ts`.\n- **Test:** I updated the key-order assertion in `test/app.test.ts` to expect both keys.\n- **Your call:** If you'd rather have a clean rename, the contract needs changing on the `web-storefront` side first, and I haven't touched that.\n- **Blocked command:** One shell command I tried was denied for needing approval. It didn't run or change anything, and I made the edits with the edit tool instead.",
